&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q&amp;amp;A:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q: Can I replace a blurb that you wrote for one of my articles with my own? I&#039;m not satisfied with it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A: Absolutely. You will always have that option at any point.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q: I noticed an error/typo/incorrect information and wish to correct it. May I?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A: Sure! If the changes are not limited to your own article(s) and/or are substantial changes across multiple entries, you should post in that month&#039;s discussion page and then make the changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span&gt;Q: I wrote an article and it seems to have stuck. Can I send a blurb of mine to one of the frequent collaborators?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A: Yup! It&#039;s much easier if you come to us about it, and it gives you the control over what you want shown on the news page.&lt;/p&gt;
